course: dictionary
lesson: 5062
title: Looking closely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inspect is a useful word because it shows up in science, safety and school life. To inspect something means to look at it closely and carefully, to check it or find faults. «Engineers inspect them regularly» tells you the engineers look at old bridges and buildings again and again to keep them safe.
explain: The word can also mean an official visit. Inspectors visit schools to check that they are run properly. Look at the clues around the word: if the sentence is about checking a place, the meaning is probably the official visit.
explain: Context helps again. «Some robot dogs inspect places too dangerous for people» tells you the robot is doing the looking. Try your meaning in the sentence: "some robot dogs look carefully at places too dangerous for people." That fits, so inspect means to look at something closely to check it.
fact: Inspect means to look at something closely and carefully to check it or find faults.
fact: «Old bridges and buildings can weaken over time, so engineers inspect them regularly» means they check the bridges and buildings often, so any damage is found early.
fact: Inspect can also mean an official visit to check that a place, like a school or restaurant, is run properly.
fact: Phrases you may meet include inspect closely, inspect for damage and inspect the troops.
fact: In science, you might inspect a leaf with a magnifying glass to see its tiny details.
exercise: «Engineers inspect old bridges regularly.» What does inspect mean here? | To paint them bright colours | To knock them down quickly | To count the cars that cross them | *To check them carefully for problems
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Old bridges and buildings can weaken over time, so engineers inspect them regularly» that means often, at set times. | time | *regularly | engineers | old
exercise: Inspectors visit schools to check they are run properly. What is the job of an inspector? | Someone who cleans the classrooms | Someone who teaches the youngest class | Someone who sells school dinners | *Someone who makes an official visit to check a place is run properly
test: «The robot dog will inspect the cave for danger before the rescue team goes in.» What does inspect mean here? | To hide from the cave | *To look carefully to check for danger | To jump over the cave | To sing loudly at the cave
test: Which phrase means to look closely for damage? | Run away quickly | *Inspect for damage | Paint the wall | Sleep for hours
exam: Which sentence uses inspect correctly? | The bird will inspect the sun before it sings. | Dad will inspect the kettle by boiling the sky. | *I will inspect my bike for loose brakes before I ride it. | We inspect our lunch by eating it in the park.
